IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 6, the subsection pass 1 left unencoded (pass 2).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Section 29(2) says that s 29's deeming of service by post leaves section 160 of the Evidence Act 1995
-- working. Pass 1 left it inert as "refers to another Act"; that is not a ground for leaving a provision out, and the subsection has an
-- answer a person can test: whether s 29 stops s 160 from operating. The rule for s 29(1) is in au-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `Part 6: Service of documents (section 29(2))`

§§ `Section 29(2): the Evidence Act 1995 still operates`

-- Whether section 160 of the Evidence Act 1995 would operate on the document is an INPUT: that section is not in the text.
-- src:622 | (2) This section does not affect the operation of section 160 of the Evidence Act 1995.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 29(2) (src:622)
GIVEN `section 160 of the Evidence Act 1995 would operate on the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 29 stops section 160 of the Evidence Act 1995 operating` `section 160 of the Evidence Act 1995 would operate on the document` MEANS
    IF `section 160 of the Evidence Act 1995 would operate on the document`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
